# What is a QALY, and why do we need it?
prompt: "Why isn't 'extra years of life' enough to compare two treatments? How does the QALY combine quantity and quality of life into one number? What does it mean for a health state to be valued at 0.6 rather than 1.0?"
comments: {"repoId":"R_kgDOUIbP1A","category":"Announcements","categoryId":"DIC_kwDOUIbP1M4DEv5x"}
next: {"title":"How is a QALY actually calculated?","href":"https://drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/dcast/understanding-the-qaly/how-is-a-qaly-actually-calculated.cast"}
enroll: https://drawcast.anvil.app

## Not All Years Are Equal
level: basic
domain: {"x":[58,71],"y":[0,9],"box":"full"}

    arrow timeline #8f887c from.data [60,7.5] to.data [69,7.5] hidden true
    label label_age60 "Age 60" above-left attach_to timeline hidden true
    icon patient_icon at.data [60,8.4] size 150 of user hidden true
    path bar_hip closed #b5482e points [[60,4.5],[65,4.5],[65,5.3],[60,5.3]] data true style.fill #b5482e style.fill_style hatch style.opacity 0.55 hidden true
    label label_hip_name "Hip" left attach_to bar_hip hidden true
    label label_hip_years "5 years" right attach_to bar_hip hidden true
    label label_hip_quality "Daily pain" below attach_to bar_hip hidden true
    path bar_drug closed #2f6b8f points [[60,1.4],[67,1.4],[67,2.2],[60,2.2]] data true style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.7 hidden true
    path tick_1 thick #173f57 points [[61,1.35],[61,2.25]] data true hidden true
    path tick_2 thick #173f57 points [[62,1.35],[62,2.25]] data true hidden true
    path tick_3 thick #173f57 points [[63,1.35],[63,2.25]] data true hidden true
    path tick_4 thick #173f57 points [[64,1.35],[64,2.25]] data true hidden true
    path tick_5 thick #173f57 points [[65,1.35],[65,2.25]] data true hidden true
    path tick_6 thick #173f57 points [[66,1.35],[66,2.25]] data true hidden true
    group drug_ticks members ["tick_1","tick_2","tick_3","tick_4","tick_5","tick_6"] hidden true
    label label_drug_name "Drug therapy" left attach_to bar_drug hidden true
    label label_drug_years "7 years" right attach_to bar_drug hidden true
    label label_drug_quality "Side effects" below attach_to bar_drug hidden true
    icon policy_icon top-right size 50 of clipboard style.opacity 0.5 hidden true
    label policy_label "Used in health policy" below #8f887c attach_to policy_icon style.opacity 0.5 hidden true

    card title "Not All Years Are Equal"

Imagine a 60-year-old choosing between a hip replacement and a drug that fights her disease.
    draw timeline label_age60 patient_icon

    pause 1

The hip replacement gives her five more years, but with pain in the joint every day.
    draw bar_hip label_hip_name label_hip_years label_hip_quality

    pause 1

The drug gives her seven more years, but its side effects leave her tired and unwell.
    draw bar_drug drug_ticks label_drug_name label_drug_years label_drug_quality policy_icon policy_label

    pause 1

So which treatment is really better — the one with more years, or the one with better years?
    arrow bracket_quantity dashed #8f887c from.data [60,6.2] to.data [67,6.2]
    label label_quantity "Quantity" above attach_to bracket_quantity
    arrow bracket_quality dashed #8f887c from.data [60,0.6] to.data [67,0.6]
    label label_quality "Quality" below attach_to bracket_quality
    dot q_anchor at.data [63.5,3] style.opacity 0
    label q_mark "?" above #8a5fa8 attach_to q_anchor font_size 60
    parallel true

    highlight bar_hip bar_drug effect glow

## Weighing the Years
level: basic

    pieces bar_hip #b5482e x 230 y 400 width 380 height 220 n 5 of strips style.fill #b5482e hidden true
    pieces bar_drug #2f6b8f x 700 y 400 width 500 height 220 n 7 of strips style.fill #2f6b8f hidden true
    label label_hip "Hip replacement" below attach_to bar_hip hidden true
    label label_drug "Drug therapy" below attach_to bar_drug hidden true
    math eq tex "QALY = \\sum_t u_t \\times t" size 34 colors.u_t #8a5fa8 x 500 y 660 hidden true

    card title "Weighing the Years"

Now that we've seen why counting years alone misses something, we can fix it by weighing each year by how good it feels.
    draw bar_hip label_hip bar_drug label_drug

    pause 1

Economists call this weight u_t — a number between 0 and 1 that scores the quality of a year.
    label w_hip "0.7" above #b5482e attach_to bar_hip
    label w_drug "0.5" above #2f6b8f attach_to bar_drug
    parallel true

    pause 1

Multiply the years by their quality weight, and add them up: QALY equals the sum of u_t times time in that state.
    draw eq

    pause 1

Suddenly, five painful years and seven tiring years become numbers we can actually compare.
    morph eq tex "QALY = 0.7\\times5 + 0.5\\times7 = 3.5 + 3.5"

    highlight eq effect pulse

## What 0.6 Feels Like
level: basic

    path axis thick #3d3833 details "Agencies like NICE in the UK use a scale exactly like this one to decide which treatments the health service should pay for — without a common yardstick, a year of pain relief and a year of extra life simply cannot be weighed against each other." points [[380,100],[380,660]] hidden true
    path tick_bottom thick #3d3833 points [[345,100],[415,100]] hidden true
    path tick_top thick #3d3833 points [[345,660],[415,660]] hidden true
    label label_bottom "0 = dead" left attach_to tick_bottom font_size 32 hidden true
    label label_top "1 = full health" left attach_to tick_top font_size 32 hidden true
    dot marker_06 #2f6b8f at.x 380 at.y 480 hidden true
    path tick_06 #2f6b8f points [[360,480],[400,480]] hidden true
    label value_06 "0.6" left #2f6b8f attach_to marker_06 font_size 30 hidden true
    shape hip_head #2f6b8f shape circle x 650 y 548 radius 14 hidden true
    path hip_body thick #2f6b8f points [[650,534],[650,485]] hidden true
    path hip_arms thick #2f6b8f points [[625,505],[675,505]] hidden true
    path hip_leg1 thick #2f6b8f points [[650,485],[630,450]] hidden true
    path hip_leg2 smooth thick #2f6b8f points [[650,485],[670,460],[660,445]] hidden true
    group icon_hip members ["hip_head","hip_body","hip_arms","hip_leg1","hip_leg2"] hidden true
    label label_hip "Hip replacement — limp" below #2f6b8f attach_to icon_hip font_size 28 hidden true
    dot marker_05 #b5482e at.x 380 at.y 230 hidden true
    path tick_05 #b5482e points [[360,230],[400,230]] hidden true
    label value_05 "0.5" left #b5482e attach_to marker_05 font_size 30 hidden true
    shape drug_head #b5482e shape circle x 650 y 298 radius 14 hidden true
    path drug_body smooth thick #b5482e points [[650,284],[638,245]] hidden true
    path drug_arm1 thick #b5482e points [[638,260],[615,255]] hidden true
    path drug_arm2 thick #b5482e points [[638,260],[650,235]] hidden true
    path drug_leg1 thick #b5482e points [[638,245],[620,210]] hidden true
    path drug_leg2 thick #b5482e points [[638,245],[645,210]] hidden true
    group icon_drug members ["drug_head","drug_body","drug_arm1","drug_arm2","drug_leg1","drug_leg2"] hidden true
    label label_drug "Drug — fatigue" below #b5482e attach_to icon_drug font_size 28 hidden true
    group scale_fig members ["axis","tick_bottom","tick_top","label_bottom","label_top","marker_06","tick_06","value_06","icon_hip","label_hip","marker_05","tick_05","value_05","icon_drug","label_drug"] fit full hidden true

    card title "What 0.6 Feels Like"

Now that we have the formula, what does a weight like 0.6 actually mean?
    draw axis tick_bottom tick_top

    pause 1

The scale runs from 0, meaning dead, to 1, meaning full health, with everything else in between.
    draw label_bottom label_top

    pause 1

A year at 0.6 is worth six-tenths of a year in full health — moderate pain, but still very much a life worth living.
    draw marker_06 tick_06 value_06 icon_hip label_hip

    pause 1

That single number lets us say exactly how much a year of hip pain costs, compared to a year of full health.
    draw marker_05 tick_05 value_05 icon_drug label_drug

    pause 1

    highlight marker_06 marker_05 effect circle

## One Number, One Comparison
level: basic

    shape hip_bar #b5482e shape rect x 280 y 600 width 240 height 140 style.fill #b5482e style.opacity 0.7 hidden true
    shape drug_bar #2f6b8f shape rect x 620 y 600 width 320 height 140 style.fill #2f6b8f style.opacity 0.5 hidden true
    label hip_seg_label "5 yrs, u = 0.7" above attach_to hip_bar hidden true
    label drug_seg_label "7 yrs, u = 0.5" above attach_to drug_bar hidden true
    math formula tex "QALY = \\sum_t u_t \\times t" x 450 y 430 hidden true
    shape hip_total_box shape rect x 280 y 260 width 10 height 10 style.opacity 0 hidden true
    shape drug_total_box shape rect x 620 y 260 width 10 height 10 style.opacity 0 hidden true
    label hip_total "Hip: 3.5 QALYs" below #b5482e attach_to hip_total_box hidden true
    label drug_total "Drug: 3.75 QALYs" below #2f6b8f attach_to drug_total_box hidden true
    icon clipboard size 100 set lucide x 450 y 140 of clipboard-check hidden true
    label clipboard_label "Health agency" below attach_to clipboard hidden true
    arrow arrow_hip_total #b5482e from.anchor bottom from.ref hip_bar to.anchor top to.ref hip_total_box hidden true
    arrow arrow_drug_total #2f6b8f from.anchor bottom from.ref drug_bar to.anchor top to.ref drug_total_box hidden true
    mark insight_mark around hip_total drug_total kind box hidden true
    text equals_sign "=" #8f887c x 430 y 600 font_size 40 hidden true

    card title "One Number, One Comparison"

Now that we can see what each weight means, the two treatments finally speak the same language.
    draw hip_bar drug_bar hip_seg_label drug_seg_label equals_sign parallel true

    pause 1

Five years at 0.7 and seven years at 0.5 turn into 3.5 and 3.75 QALYs — comparable numbers, not just guesses.
    draw arrow_hip_total arrow_drug_total formula hip_total drug_total

    pause 1

Health agencies use exactly this kind of number to decide which treatments are worth funding.
    draw clipboard clipboard_label parallel true

    pause 1

So the answer to our first question is simple: it's not more years or better years alone — it's both, multiplied together, that the QALY lets us see.
    draw insight_mark

